              <div class="stat-tile"><b>1300+</b><span>Projects completed</span></div>
              <div class="stat-tile"><b>Full</b><span>Workmanship warranty</span></div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="projects">Bathroom projects we take on</h2>
            <p>Whether you are refreshing a tired hall bath or building a spa-like primary suite, we scope the project to your house and to how your household actually uses the room:</p>

            <div class="pj-grid">
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Tub-to-shower conversion</h3>
                <p>Trade the alcove tub nobody has used in fifteen years for a roomy, easy-to-clean walk-in shower — same footprint, no structural work, and the most requested bathroom upgrade in Bradenton and Sarasota. <a href="/blog/tub-to-shower-conversion-bradenton/">What a conversion involves</a>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Walk-in &amp; custom showers</h3>
                <p>Curbless entries, linear drains, large-format tile, benches, lighted niches and frameless glass — plus the waterproofing details that decide whether a shower lasts five years or twenty-five. <a href="/services/custom-showers/">Custom shower installation</a>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Primary bath suites</h3>
                <p>Twin vanities, a freestanding soaking tub, a separate walk-in shower, and a layout that finally makes sense instead of a corner garden tub eating the middle of the room — designed and built as one room.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Guest &amp; powder rooms</h3>
                <p>Smaller-scope refreshes and full remodels for hall baths, guest baths and half-baths that still deserve to be done right — the honest option when the layout already works and the waterproofing is what aged out.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Accessible &amp; aging-in-place</h3>
                <p>Zero-threshold showers, real blocking set in the walls for grab bars, comfort-height fixtures and slip-resistant tile — accessibility that reads as a well-designed bathroom, not an institutional one.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pj-c">
                <h3>Full bathroom remodels</h3>
                <p>Down-to-the-studs remodels with a new layout, plumbing and electrical, <a href="/services/tile-natural-stone/">tile and stone</a>, vanity, lighting and <a href="/services/flooring/">flooring</a>, coordinated start to finish on one contract.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="why-vl-pro">Why homeowners choose VL Pro</h2>
            <p>There are a lot of remodelers between Palmetto and Venice. Here is what actually differs about working with us:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>One in-house crew.</strong> The same people demo the room and set the last piece of trim. No subcontractor handoffs, and nobody blaming the last trade.</li>
              <li><strong>One point of contact.</strong> The person who quotes your bathroom is the person running it. You get their number, not a dispatch line.</li>
              <li><strong>Fixed scope, priced before demo.</strong> The whole scope is priced up front — no allowances that balloon, and no change order that arrives without a photo of what we found attached to it.</li>
              <li><strong>Schluter®-certified waterproofing.</strong> Every pan is built on a certified membrane and flood-tested for 24 hours before a single tile goes on.</li>
              <li><strong>Permits pulled and inspected.</strong> We file as the licensed contractor of record with Manatee County, Sarasota County or your city building department, and we meet the inspector.</li>
              <li><strong>Certified for the surfaces we install.</strong> Large-format tile, natural stone, XL porcelain slab, glass tile and art glass panel, and members of the National Tile Contractors Association.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="process">How your bathroom comes together</h2>
            <p>Every bathroom we build runs through the same four phases, so you always know where the project stands and what happens next.</p>

            <div class="steps">
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
                <h3>Free consultation &amp; detailed estimate</h3>
                <p>We come to the house, measure the room, check what the plumbing and framing will actually allow, and talk through budget and timeline honestly. You leave with an itemized scope, a price and a start date — not a range. No cost, no obligation.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
                <h3>Design, selections &amp; permit</h3>
                <p>Tile, vanity, countertop, fixtures, lighting and paint are chosen and ordered before anything comes apart, so decisions happen on paper rather than mid-build when changes get expensive. If the layout moves plumbing, we pull the permit while the materials are in transit.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
                <h3>Demo, rough-in &amp; waterproofing</h3>
                <p>The room comes down to the studs. We repair the subfloor, set the new plumbing and electrical rough-in, then build and flood-test the waterproofing assembly before the inspector signs it off. Floors and hallways are protected, dust is contained, and the debris leaves with us.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <span class="step-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
                <h3>Finish &amp; walkthrough</h3>
                <p>Tile goes in, grout is sealed, the vanity and fixtures are set, and the glass goes in last, measured off finished tile rather than off the framing. We clean the room, walk it with you, and fix everything on your list before we call it done.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2 id="cost">What a bathroom remodel costs in Bradenton and Sarasota</h2>
            <p>Bathroom cost comes down to three things: the size of the room, the materials you choose, and whether the plumbing or the layout has to move. Most remodels in this market run between <strong>$18,000 and $45,000</strong> and take three to eight weeks. These are typical ranges for our area — your estimate is built to your actual room.</p>

            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Scope</th><th>Typical range</th><th>Timeline</th><th>Includes</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Focused refresh</td>
                  <td>$18K – $26K</td>
                  <td>3–5 weeks</td>
                  <td>New vanity, countertop, floor and wall tile, fixtures and lighting, with the existing layout kept.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><span class="row-us">Full remodel</span></td>
                  <td>$26K – $38K</td>
                  <td>4–6 weeks</td>
                  <td>The above plus a walk-in shower or tub-to-shower conversion, tile surround, linear drain and frameless glass.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Primary suite</td>
                  <td>$38K and up</td>
                  <td>6–8 weeks</td>
                  <td>Layout changes, twin vanities, custom shower, freestanding tub, heated floor and premium finishes.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <blockquote>
              <p><strong>The one thing that moves the number most:</strong> whether you keep the existing plumbing locations. Nearly every home here is slab-on-grade, so relocating a toilet or a shower drain means cutting and re-pouring concrete plus extra permitting — often the difference between a $26K and a $40K bathroom of the same finish quality. We price both versions at the walkthrough so you can spend where it matters to you.</p>
            </blockquote>

            <h2 id="finishes">Finishes and the details that last</h2>
            <p>A bathroom looks new on day one; the question is how it looks in fifteen years. On the Gulf Coast that comes down to what happens behind the tile as much as the tile itself. A bathroom in this climate never fully dries out between uses, so we build a continuous waterproof system in every wet zone — not sealed grout and caulk — tie it in at the corners and transitions, and flood-test it before tile. The exhaust fan gets sized and ducted to the outside rather than into the attic, and we will not set tile over a substrate that is not rated for it.</p>
            <p>Above the waterline it is layout work: tile set to a planned grid so the cuts land where nobody looks, mitered edges instead of bullnose trim, niches lined up with the courses around them. For the finishes you see, we walk the showrooms with you so you can touch the material before anything is ordered. Near the water we specify fixtures and glass hardware that can take salt air without pitting inside two seasons.</p>

            <h2 id="offer">Save on your project</h2>
            <h3>$1000 off your remodel, plus a free in-home design consultation</h3>
            <p>Ask about the current offer when you book. Terms and restrictions apply, and it is valid on projects over $10,000. The in-home design consultation is free either way — we sit down with you and plan layout and fixture placement, tile, vanity and finishes, permits and inspections, and the budget and timeline, before you commit to anything.</p>

